?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-24T07:05:29Z","updated_at":"2025-06-24T07:05:29Z","body":"Personally, I'm not sure that using UIDs in human-created and human-readable files like scripts is a good idea. It hurts readability/accessibility and makes it hard to find bugs, even if the original file path is specified in a comment.\n\nIn my opinion, if we should support UIDs, it should be paired with the file path, as an optional fallback/integrity control measure (second optional argument to `load()`, `preload()`, `extends`), see the [comment](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/87418#issuecomment-1907516677). But it seems like my opinion doesn't have much support, so I don't mind this fix.\n\nSee also:\n\n* #87418\n* #87454\n* #87488\n\nCC @KoBeWi","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2999082958/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2999105427","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103479#issuecomment-2999105427","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103479","id":2999105427,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ywreT","user":{"login":"4d49","id":8208165,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgyMDgxNjU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8208165?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/4d49","html_url":"https://github.com/4d49","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/4d49/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/4d49/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/4d49/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/4d49/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/4d49/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/4d49/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/4d49/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/4d49/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/4d49/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-24T07:13:32Z","updated_at":"2025-06-24T07:13:32Z","body":"> Personally, I'm not sure that using UIDs in human-created and human-readable files like scripts is a good idea. It hurts readability/accessibility and makes it hard to find bugs, even if the original file path is specified in a comment.\n> \nThis allows you not to care about the specific location of the script file. Besides, it can improve mod support, right?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2999105427/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2999232866","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103479#issuecomment-2999232866","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103479","id":2999232866,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yxKli","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-24T07:57:21Z","updated_at":"2025-06-24T07:57:21Z","body":"Extending by UID was working after #101442, but then something broke it again. UID extend has the same level of readability as preload by UID, so I don't see why it should be disallowed. You can hover the UID to see its path.\n\n> In my opinion, if we should support UIDs, it should be paired with the file path\n\nYeah, optional path makes sense.\n\n> Besides, it can improve mod support, right?\n\nIt does not really affect mod support. With `take_over_path()` you can freely manage Resource's path and their real location does not matter.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2999232866/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3262326699","html_url":"htt